menu "ESP Wi-Fi Connect (local fork)"

    config WIFI_CONNECT_PORTAL_CHECK
        bool "Detect and pass captive portals after connecting"
        default n
        help
            After the station gets an IP address, request a small connectivity-check page. When a
            login page (public, hotel or school Wi-Fi) is in the way, fill it with the account saved
            for the network, then announce the connection. Costs a short HTTP request on every
            connect and sends it to connectivitycheck.gstatic.com, so it is off by default. A board
            enables it through the sdkconfig lines of its config.json. NVS wifi/portal_check
            (0 or 1) overrides this default at run time.

endmenu
